  "author": "Ian Anstice / The Library Campaign",
  "editorial": {
    "text": "My thanks to Liz White of the British Library for answering my many questions about the much-awaited Single Digital Presence below. In other news, there’s a couple of possible new cuts (Bolton and the Isle of Man), a library closed for reapirs, and two stories of closires/co-locations from Scotland. But, frankly, we’re all waiting for what Mr Johnson announces tomorrow and whether children’s events in English libraries this August will be a thing or not.",
    "html": "<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">My thanks to Liz White of the British Library for answering my many questions about the much-awaited Single Digital Presence below. In other news, there&#8217;s a couple of possible new cuts (Bolton and the Isle of Man), a library closed for reapirs, and two stories of closires/co-locations from Scotland. But, frankly, we&#8217;re all waiting for what Mr Johnson announces tomorrow and whether children&#8217;s events in English libraries this August will be a thing or not. </p>"
  },
